[223] (w=71) Partially yes, but [1mnot true Omarchy[22m. Omarchy's defining features live  [0m]8;;
[224] (w=71) in layers Apple containers abstract away (bootloader, full-disk LUKS,  [0m]8;;
[225] (w=71) btrfs root, x86-64 desktop). You can build an [1mArch container image and [0m]8;;
[226] (w=71) [1minstall most of the Omarchy userland[22m, but it becomes an                [0m]8;;
[227] (w=71) "Omarchy-flavored Arch dev VM," not the bootable FDE desktop.          [0m]8;;
[228] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[229] (w=71) [38;2;250;204;110m[1mWhat the manual install actually demands[22m[39m                               [0m]8;;
[230] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[231] (w=71) The installer isn't a package script — it hard-requires a specific     [0m]8;;
[232] (w=71) prebuilt machine. Relevant guards from [38;2;218;186;250mpreflight/guard.sh[39m:             [0m]8;;
[233] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[234] (w=71) ┌─────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┐[0m]8;;
[235] (w=71) │ [1mGuard              [22m │ [1mIn Apple container                           [22m │[0m]8;;
[236] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[237] (w=71) │ [38;2;218;186;250m/etc/arch-release[39m[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m   │ ✅ if you use Arch image                      │[0m]8;;
[238] (w=71) │ exists              │                                               │[0m]8;;
[239] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[240] (w=71) │ Must not run as[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m     │ ✅ make a user                                │[0m]8;;
[241] (w=71) │ root                │                                               │[0m]8;;
[242] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[243] (w=71) │ [1m[38;2;218;186;250muname -m[39m == [38;2;218;186;250mx86_64[39m[22m  │ ⚠️ Omarchy is x86-only. On Apple Silicon you[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m  │[0m]8;;
[244] (w=71) │                     │ must build the image as [38;2;218;186;250m--arch amd64[39m and run[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m  │[0m]8;;
[245] (w=71) │                     │ it under Rosetta. Then the [3mwhole guest[23m is[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m     │[0m]8;;
[246] (w=71) │                     │ x86_64 and this guard passes.                 │[0m]8;;
[247] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[248] (w=71) │ Secure Boot[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m         │ ✅ no-op in container                         │[0m]8;;
[249] (w=71) │ disabled            │                                               │[0m]8;;
[250] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[251] (w=71) │ No Gnome/KDE[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m        │ ✅                                            │[0m]8;;
[252] (w=71) │ preinstalled        │                                               │[0m]8;;
[253] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[254] (w=71) │ [38;2;218;186;250mlimine[39m on PATH      │ ✅ pacman installable, but pointless          │[0m]8;;
[255] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[256] (w=71) │ [1mroot is btrfs[22m       │ ❌ container root is the content-store fs,[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m    │[0m]8;;
[257] (w=71) │                     │ not btrfs. This tripped                       │[0m]8;;
[258] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[259] (w=71) │ Limine bootloader   │ meaningless in a VM                           │[0m]8;;
[260] (w=71) ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤[0m]8;;
[261] (w=71) │ Non-root [38;2;218;186;250m--now[39m[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m      │ fix with [38;2;218;186;250mOMARCHY_CHROOT_INSTALL=1[39m (swaps[22;23;24;25;27;28;29;39m      │[0m]8;;
[262] (w=71) │ service starts      │ [38;2;218;186;250msystemctl enable --now[39m → [38;2;218;186;250menable[39m)              │[0m]8;;
[263] (w=71) └─────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┘[0m]8;;
[264] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[265] (w=71) Every guard is technically beatable — [38;2;218;186;250mabort()[39m just does a [38;2;218;186;250mgum confirm  [0m]8;;
[266] (w=71) [38;2;218;186;250m"proceed anyway?"[39m. But the guards aren't the blocker; what comes [3mafter[23m [0m]8;;
[267] (w=71) them is.                                                               [0m]8;;
[268] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[269] (w=71) [38;2;250;204;110m[1mThe real showstoppers[22m[39m                                                  [0m]8;;
[270] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[271] (w=71) The [38;2;218;186;250mlogin/[39m module (run on every install) assumes real boot hardware:   [0m]8;;
[272] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[273] (w=71) [38;2;218;186;250m- [39m[1mlimine-snapper.sh[22m: writes mkinitcpio hook ([38;2;218;186;250mencrypt btrfs-overlayfs   [0m]8;;
[274] (w=71)   [38;2;218;186;250mplymouth[39m), rebuilds UKIs, runs [38;2;218;186;250mlimine-update[39m, [38;2;218;186;250mefibootmgr[39m against     [0m]8;;
[275] (w=71)   NVRAM, [38;2;218;186;250msnapper create-config /[39m and [38;2;218;186;250mbtrfs quota disable /[39m. In a       [0m]8;;
[276] (w=71)   container: no [38;2;218;186;250m/boot/EFI[39m, no ESP, no NVRAM, root isn't btrfs →        [0m]8;;
[277] (w=71)   snapper/limine-update fail. Several branches [38;2;218;186;250mexit 1[39m, and the         [0m]8;;
[278] (w=71)   installer runs under [38;2;218;186;250mset -eEo pipefail[39m → [1mwhole install aborts[22m.       [0m]8;;
[279] (w=71) [38;2;218;186;250m- [39m[1mhibernation.sh / sddm.sh[22m: need LUKS/swap/resume and a real display   [0m]8;;
[280] (w=71)   session. Dead in a headless VM.                                      [0m]8;;
[281] (w=71) [38;2;218;186;250m- [39m[1mThe core security model[22m (auto-login only after LUKS decrypt at boot) [0m]8;;
[282] (w=71)   is an initramfs/bootloader concept. Containers have no equivalent.   [0m]8;;
[283] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
[284] (w=71) Plymouth theming and most of [38;2;218;186;250mconfig/[39m and [38;2;218;186;250mpackaging/[39m are fine.          [0m]8;;
[285] (w=71)                                                                        [0m]8;;
